From c566f187f8d00b33a7f9c1eb61dd660b15c45d1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:51:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MSI M1: MSI-X capability on the xHCI (QEMU shape)

0:20.0 now exposes the capability list qemu-xhci wears: Status bit 4,
Capabilities Pointer 0x90, MSI-X capability (ID 0x11, Table Size 16)
with the vector table at BAR0+0x3000 and the PBA at BAR0+0x3800
(MSI_PLAN 1b).  The default PCI config write path is fully writable,
so xhci_pci_cfg_write re-asserts every read-only field after each
write and folds Message Control's two RW bits (Enable, Function
Mask) into xhci_t, where the M3 router will read them.

The table is live MMIO storage in xhci_t (16 x addr_lo/addr_hi/data/
ctrl), all entries masked at power-on; the PBA reads 0 and ignores
writes (v1 keeps no pending accumulation -- a level-signalled source
re-evaluates on unmask, MSI_PLAN section 2).  Because MSI-X state is
PCI-function state, xhci_hw_reset now preserves the table and both
control bits across HCRST, like the BAR decode; snapshots carry it
inside xhci_t as before.  Nothing routes yet: INTx delivery is
untouched (M2/M3).

tests/test_xhci.c gains v_msix_cap (23 groups): the capability walk
through real 0xCF8/0xCFC, a blast-write RO audit, table round-trips
incl. entry 15 and the past-the-end read, PBA zero, and HCRST
persistence.  NC: src/xhci.c + src/devices.c at M0 -> 13 failures.
Gates: make test, make test-sanitize, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.
